<title>CANADA: British Columbia criticizes Canada federal budget.</title>
<headline>British Columbia criticizes Canada federal budget.</headline>
<dateline>VICTORIA, British Columbia 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Columbia Premier Glen Clark on Tuesday called Canada's new federal budget disappointing.</p>
<p>&quot;I am disappointed in one major thing and that is there is no job strategy,&quot; Clark told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;I accept that the deficit is down. That is good news. (But) they have made a very tepid start on child poverty. The thing the budget fails to do more than anything else is give any hope for the unemployment rate,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Liberal Finance Minister Paul Martin tabled the 1997/98 federal budget earlier in Ottawa.</p>
<p>((Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314))</p>
